Z||000006||Shaun41178||11-26-2001||09:38 PM||||Formula, Wade ddn't notice a difference.  It was just psychological to him.  I dont' think he felt a torque increase of 2-4 lb-ft.  Do you?  His @ss-meter is way off.  Noone can feel that.  Its like someone saying they felt a difference from a chip for a Fiero.  No you didn't.  Why?  Cause they don't add any power!!  I have seen dyno graphs.<P>I installed my pulley and didn't notice any difference.  I never had it dynoed though but it does give several hp up top oh say around 5500-6k rpm.<P>How come many fiero owners use the butt meter and not an actual dyno?  Stop being cheapos and spreading false info based on your @ss meters.  God I hate it when people do that.<P>Read <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/FieroGtNOS" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/FieroGtNOS</A>   and look for the link on my pulley install.  Maybe something can be learned from that and not to trust your @ss meter.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||13
