Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||11-27-2001||10:59 AM||||Sheesh Shaun, you really should lighten up a little.  As he re-stated above, he never said that it produced more TQ or HP, just liked the way it felt!  There are days that my GT feels sluggish, and others when it feels like the fastest its ever been.  Has nothing to do with the actual power output of the engine or overall vehicle setup.  Just simply the feel of the ride... how nice & firmly it puts you back in your seat.<P>I have upgraded my car (3.1, intake/TB, etc...)- I have an ADS Chip (not yet installed), I'm planning the pulley upgrade, as well as &lt;gasp&gt; probably a shiny cold air intake system. All purely for for the knowelege that they're there.  Even if I only get .5 HP more from any given mod, that's .5HP I didn't have before. They all add up in the end.  I just love the way my car drives, not necessarily based the numbers it can produce on a $50/hour dyno!<P>As you know, I bought a G-Tech computer from you for the purpose of finding out some rough 0-60 and HP numbers for my GT, strangely enough I never quite found the time to get those numbers before it started snowing... so I guess I'll just have to wait until next season.  No biggie.<P>And Shaun- I'm not intending this as a flame towards you, you're really a nice person and I quite enjoy my dealings with you.  But you've seemed really tense and quick to jump on people in their posts as of late (turbo & performance stuff especially).  In a forum, the same question may be asked a thousand times, and I prefer to just keep re-answering them (or at least directing them to whatever thread I feel might already contain the answer they're looking for).  Just relax, have fun, and enjoy your car!<P>And Sorry everyone for my long ranting post... I just felt I needed to say all that.||||reg||1
